course: dictionary
lesson: 11647
title: Artful: clever or sneaky?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Artful is an adjective. It describes a person, an animal, or something they do. An artful person is clever at getting what they want, often by tricking people. «The artful fox crept past the hens without waking the farmer.» The fox is clever, but its cleverness is sneaky.
explain: Artful can also mean done with great skill and cleverness, and then it is praise. «The artful design had tiny silver stars on every page.» Nobody is being tricked here. The word tells you the design is clever and well made.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the clues around the word. Is someone being tricked, or is something being made well? In The Wind in the Willows, the stoats and weasels are artful because they trick their way into things, and Toad is artful in his disguises. Always ask: is this clever in a good way, or clever in a sneaky way?
fact: Artful means clever at getting what you want, especially by tricking people; crafty.
fact: Artful can also mean done with skill and cleverness, as in «an artful design».
fact: The Artful Dodger is a young pickpocket in the story Oliver Twist.
fact: Artful is an adjective, so its forms are artful, more artful, and most artful.
fact: When artful means tricking, it is usually a warning; when it means skill, it is praise.
exercise: «The artful cat waited quietly until the mouse came out, then pounced.» What does artful suggest about the cat? | *Clever at tricking others to get what it wants | Afraid of mice | Sleepy and slow | Loud and clumsy
exercise: «Her artful drawing of the castle had curled towers and tiny windows.» What does artful mean here? | Sneaky and dishonest | Very messy and rushed | *Done with great skill and cleverness | Too big to carry
exercise: Sam says artful is always a nice word, like a compliment. Is he right? | No, it means tired and sleepy | Yes, but only when talking about dogs | Yes, it always means kind and gentle | *No, it can mean sneaky tricking, which is a warning
test: «The stoat was artful, and it tricked the rabbits into opening the gate.» What does artful mean in this sentence? | Very tired and slow | Careful with small things | *Clever at tricking others | Kind and helpful to others
test: Which meaning of artful is praise? | *Done with great skill and cleverness | Clever at tricking people | Crafty and sneaky | Quiet and shy
exam: Jayden asks, «Is artful always a bad thing?» What is the best answer? | No, because it means tired and slow | *No, it can mean skilful and clever, not only tricking | Yes, it always means sneaky and dishonest | Yes, but only in stories about animals
